NOTE: the protocol returns only the sign of the threshold test, the selected
cluster index, and the column index -- never the id of the matched record. So a
CATCH means "some record in the selected cluster scored above tau", not "the
right record was found": the recall above is a DETECTION rate, not identification
precision/recall. It also has tau in its own denominator, so raising tau moves the
hardest queries out of the denominator and pushes the number toward 100% without
fixing anything. It reports agreement with the threshold; it is not a target.
